From fd4244bf1eee3d3a7d213fe3063272d6c20539ef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 21:16:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(dsv41): keep a NaN through the indexer score ReLU, as
 DeepSeek's relu_ does

Base: the previous patch (bf16x2 epilogue and next-tile key prefetch in the dense indexer
score kernel).

Rationale:
DeepSeek's indexer takes relu_ of each head's dot product, which keeps a NaN. The score kernels
computed max(dot, 0), which drops it: a head whose index query has an infinite scale (UE8M0
0xFF, its dot NaN) contributed zero instead of turning the row's scores NaN.
test_indexer_nonfinite_query_scale has recorded this as a strict xfail since
experiments/2026-10-14-kernel-contracts, where the NaN-keeping forms TileLang could vectorize
cost 3.4-4.6% of prefill. With the bf16x2 epilogue, the ReLU is one __hmax2_nan
(max.NaN.bf16x2) at the same instruction count:
1. __tl_score_rows_dense_fast (both epilogues) uses __hmax2_nan.
2. __tl_score_row_candidates_fast (the reindex layers) takes the same bf16x2 epilogue, with
   __hmax2_nan, in place of its float2 round trip.

Quality:
Finite inputs keep their bits: scores and selections bit-identical to the previous patch at
prefill depths of 237K and 910K-token prompts, at the decode shapes of
benchmark_deepseek_v41_indexer_bound.py, and for the reindex candidate kernel at 6 and 96 rows
over a 1M-token context, with no measurable cost (candidate kernel 11.6 against 12.1 us at 6
rows, 294 against 299 us at 96). Only rows with a non-finite index query change: their scores
are NaN at every live position, as the reference's.

Tests:
- test_indexer_nonfinite_query_scale passes; its strict xfail is removed.
- test_indexer_candidates_nonfinite_query_scale (new): the same contract for the candidate
  kernel, a masked block still scoring -inf and the other rows keeping their bits.
- pytest tests/kernels/attention/test_deepseek_v41_tilelang.py -k "indexer or topk" without the
  xfail (29 passed, 1 skipped), and the candidate-kernel contract run on its own (1 passed).

Upstream status: local DeepSeek-V4.1 TileLang indexer fix for SM120/SM121.
